INT. SUDS & SPIN LAUNDROMAT - NIGHT

Dryers TUMBLE. Neon BUZZES.

DR. LENA VOSS (40s, scrubs under a parka) is on her knees beside a man crumpled against a washer. Gripping his wrist. Counting.

A STRANGER (60s, grey stubble, bleeding from the scalp) pulls the heavy door of dryer nine shut and leans on it, panting.

LENA
Stay with me. Eyes up here.

STRANGER
Name's Marcus. Not that anyone asked.

Lena pauses.

LENA
Marcus. Good. Marcus, who did this?

JOSIE (20s, hoodie, folding socks) backs away from the counter, phone raised. A tiny terrier on a leash YAPS at everyone.

JOSIE
I'm calling nine-one-one!

A dryer BANGS open. ABEL (50s, security vest) bursts through the back door, flashlight swinging.

ABEL
Nobody move!

MARCUS
Abel, he's gone out the front. Go!

Abel does not go. Officer KANE shoves through the front door, gun up, rain on his shoulders.

KANE
Police! Hands!

Everyone raises their hands except Lena, who is still pressing a folded towel to a wound.

Two teenagers by the soap machine freeze mid-chew.

This is the last time any of them will be strangers.

The dryer THUDS. Something inside it is still running.
